==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|ru|жалъ|овать}}.
{{rfe|ru|Is {{m|ru|жалъ}} a variant of {{m|ru|жаль|t=it's a pity}}? A semantic shift from "pity" > "sympathy" > "regard" > "favor, grant" seems quite possible.}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|жа́ловать}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|жа́ловать|impf|pf=пожа́ловать}}

# to [[grant]], to [[bestow]], to [[confer]], to [[reward]], to [[award]] {{qualifier|stilted style}}
# to [[favour]]/[[favor]], to [[regard]] [[with]] [[favour]]/[[favor]]; to [[like]]
#: {{uxi|ru|Его́ [[не]] [[о́чень]]-то '''жа́луют''' [[там]]|he is not very popular there.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[просить|прошу́]] [[люби́ть]] и '''жа́ловать'''|please welcome; I would like you to welcome ''(oneself or someone who is introduced)''}}
# {{lb|ru|dated}} to [[visit]], to come to see {{qualifier|stilted style or jocular}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf-intr|2a+p|жа́ловать|has_ppp=yes|has_prpp=yes}}

